// The order behind the delivery.
//
// RecordMaterialReceipt stood alone: grain arrived, somebody typed the
// quantity and maybe a price, and nothing said what had been ordered,
// from whom, at what price, or whether the delivery matched. Nobody
// could answer "what is on order" without a filing cabinet, a short
// delivery was invisible, and freight and duty sat in an expense account
// instead of in the cost of the grain — so every downstream figure was
// understated by exactly what it cost to get it to the door.

